captured
route: POST /tasks/<pod>/<id>/retry
status: 409
tack-sends: yes
note: retry of a task that is not blocked or failed (here one waiting on a person; a pending, running or done task answers the same): 409, the sentence in error; Tack takes it as 'the retry was already sent' and follows the task
command: curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:<port>/tasks/saas-dev/task-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/retry (bearer token from docket's --token-file)
docket: docket 0.3.0b1 (API 6), source checkout 1d180651
env: HOME and DOCKET_HOME (a throwaway folder), PATH, HTTP_PROXY/HTTPS_PROXY/ALL_PROXY (an unreachable loopback port); no model, no provider key
date: 2026-11-04
redacted: the scratch folder (as /scratch), timestamps (as 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z), 40-hex commit ids (as zeros), task ids (as an all-zero uuid), escalation ids (as esc-000000000000), approval and sweep-run ids (as an all-zero uuid), claimPid
